{:edb/db-before-t 1447 :edb/db-after-t 1448 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534760 50 #inst "2026-10-08T06:07:37.254Z" 13194139534760 true] [17592186082985 1100 "The position vector $\\mathbf{r}$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t > 0$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 3t^3, 2t^2\\rangle.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $\\mathbf{v}.$" 13194139534760 true] [17592186082985 1100 "The position vector $\\mathbf{r}$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t > 0$ is given by\n$\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 3t^3, 2t^2\\rangle$.\nCalculate the velocity vector $\\mathbf{v}$." 13194139534760 false] [17592186082985 1145 "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv &= \\frac{dr}{dt} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{dx}{dt}, \\frac{dy}{dt}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{d}{dt}(3t^{3}), \\frac{d}{dt}(2t^{2})⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨9t^{2}, 4t⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534760 false] [17592186082985 1145 "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9{t}^{2},\\,4t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534760 true] [17592186082986 1100 "The position vector $\\mathbf{r}$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t > 0$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 12t, 2t^3\\rangle.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $\\mathbf{v}$ at time $t=1.$" 13194139534760 true] [17592186082986 1100 "The position vector $\\mathbf{r}$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t > 0$ is given by\n$\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 12t, 2t^3\\rangle$.\nCalculate the velocity vector $\\mathbf{v}$ at time $t=1$." 13194139534760 false] [17592186082986 1145 "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv &= \\frac{dr}{dt} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{dx}{dt}, \\frac{dy}{dt}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{d}{dt}(12t), \\frac{d}{dt}(2t^{3})⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨12, 6t^{2}⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=1$, we substitute into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv(1) &= ⟨12, 6(1)^{2}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨12, 6⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534760 false] [17592186082986 1145 "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(12t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12,6{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=1$, we substitute into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =⟨12,6(1)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534760 true] [17592186082987 1100 "The position vector $\\mathbf{r}$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t > 0$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 6t^2+2, 2t^3\\rangle.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle at time $t=2.$" 13194139534760 true] [17592186082987 1100 "The position vector $\\mathbf{r}$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t > 0$ is given by\n$\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 6t^2+2, 2t^3\\rangle$.\nCalculate the speed of the particle at time $t=2$." 13194139534760 false] [17592186082987 1145 "First, we calculate the velocity vector $\\mathbf{v}$. Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv &= \\frac{dr}{dt} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{dx}{dt}, \\frac{dy}{dt}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{d}{dt}(6t^{2} + 2), \\frac{d}{dt}(2t^{3})⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨12t, 6t^{2}⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=2$, we substitute into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv(2) &= ⟨12(2), 6(2)^{2}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨24, 24⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=2$ we calculate the magnitude of $\\mathbf{v}(2)$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid v(2) \\mid &= \\sqrt{24^{2} + 24^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{2(24^{2})} \\\\\n&= 24\\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed when $t=2$ is\n\n$$\n24\\sqrt{2}\\approx 33.94\n$$\n\nto two decimal places." 13194139534760 false] [17592186082987 1145 "First, we calculate the velocity vector $\\mathbf{v}.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{2}+2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12t,6{t}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=2$, we substitute into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =⟨12(2),6(2)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨24,24⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=2$ we calculate the magnitude of $\\mathbf{v}(2),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(2)| & =\\sqrt{{24}^{2}+{24}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2({24}^{2})} \\\\  & =24\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed when $t=2$ is $24\\sqrt{2}\\approx 33.94$ to two decimal places." 13194139534760 true] [17592186082988 1100 "A particle $P$ moves in the $x$-$y$ plane (relative to a fixed origin $O$) with position vector\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle t^2-2t, t^3-3t \\rangle, \\quad t\\in[0,\\infty).\n$$\n\nCalculate the times at which the particle is stationary." 13194139534760 true] [17592186082988 1100 "A particle $P$ moves in the $x$-$y$ plane (relative to a fixed origin $O$) with position vector\n$[MATH: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle t^2-2t, t^3-3t \\rangle, \\quad t\\in[0,\\infty).]$\n\nCalculate the times at which the particle is stationary." 13194139534760 false] [17592186082988 1145 "First, we calculate the velocity vector $\\mathbf{v}$. Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv &= \\frac{dr}{dt} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{dx}{dt}, \\frac{dy}{dt}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{d}{dt}(t^{2} - 2t), \\frac{d}{dt}(t^{3} - 3t)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨2t - 2, 3t^{2} - 3⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when its velocity is zero. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv(t) &= 0 \\\\\n⟨2t - 2, 3t^{2} - 3⟩ &= ⟨0, 0⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2t - 2 &= 0⇒t = 1, \\\\\n3t^{2} - 3 &= 0⇒t = ± 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $t=-1$ is outside of the domain of $t$, so we discard it.\n\nThe solution $t=1$ is the only solution that satisfies both equations, so this is the only time when the object is stationary." 13194139534760 false] [17592186082988 1145 "First, we calculate the velocity vector $\\mathbf{v}.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-3t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when its velocity is zero. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨2t-2,3{t}^{2}-3⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2t-2 & =0\\,⇒\\,t=1, \\\\ 3{t}^{2}-3 & =0\\,⇒\\,t=\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $t=-1$ is outside of the domain of $t,$ so we discard it. \n\nThe solution $t=1$ is the only solution that satisfies both equations, so this is the only time when the object is stationary." 13194139534760 true] [17592186083162 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308247 13194139534760 true] [17592186083162 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308254 13194139534760 true] [17592186083162 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308294 13194139534760 true] [17592186083162 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308300 13194139534760 true] [17592186083166 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308261 13194139534760 true] [17592186083166 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308282 13194139534760 true] [17592186083166 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308303 13194139534760 true] [17592186083166 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308308 13194139534760 true] [17592186083166 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308325 13194139534760 true] [17592186083167 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308288 13194139534760 true] [17592186083167 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308314 13194139534760 true] [17592186083167 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308317 13194139534760 true] [17592186083167 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308332 13194139534760 true] [17592186083168 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308268 13194139534760 true] [17592186083168 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308275 13194139534760 true] [17592186083168 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308291 13194139534760 true] [17592186083168 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308321 13194139534760 true] [17592186083563 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534760 true] [17592186083563 1100 "A particle $P$ is moving in the $x$-$y$ plane. Its position vector relative to a fixed origin $O$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨{t}^{3/2}+4{t}^{2},\\,11t-1⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $v.$" 13194139534760 true] [17592186083563 1100 "A particle $P$ is moving in the $x$-$y$ plane. Its position vector relative to a fixed origin $O$ is given by\n\n$r = ⟨t^{3/2} + 4t^{2}, 11t - 1⟩, t > 0$.\nCalculate the velocity vector $v$." 13194139534760 false] [17592186083563 1145 "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3/2}+4{t}^{2}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(11t-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{t}+8t,\\,11⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534760 true] [17592186083681 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534760 true] [17592186083681 1100 "A particle $P$ moves in the $x$-$y$ plane (relative to a fixed origin $O$) with position vector\n\n$$\nr=⟨{t}^{2}{e}^{-2t},\\,(t-1)^{3}⟩,\\,t\\in [0,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate the times at which the particle is stationary." 13194139534760 true] [17592186083681 1100 "A particle $P$ moves in the $x$-$y$ plane (relative to a fixed origin $O$) with position vector\n$[MATH: r = ⟨t^{2}e^{-2t}, (t - 1)^{3}⟩, t ∈ [0, ∞).]$\n\nCalculate the times at which the particle is stationary." 13194139534760 false] [17592186083681 1145 "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}{e}^{-2t}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-1)^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t{e}^{-2t}-2{t}^{2}{e}^{-2t},3(t-1)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t(1-t){e}^{-2t},3(t-1)^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when its velocity is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨2t(1-t){e}^{-2t},3(t-1)^{2}⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2t(1-t){e}^{-2t}=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=0,1, \\\\ 3(t-1)^{2}=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $t=1$ is the only solution that satisfies both equations, so this is the only value of $t$ when the particle is stationary." 13194139534760 true] [17592186083833 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534760 true] [17592186083833 1100 "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2},\\,3t+7⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle at time $t=4.$" 13194139534760 true] [17592186083833 1100 "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$r = ⟨\\frac{t^{2}}{2}, 3t + 7⟩, t > 0$.\nCalculate the speed of the particle at time $t = 4$." 13194139534760 false] [17592186083833 1145 "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t+7)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=4,$ we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\nv=⟨4,3⟩\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=4$ we calculate the magnitude of $v(4),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(4)| & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed when $t=4$ is $5.$" 13194139534760 true] [17592186308247 1017 #edb/ref 17592186308248 13194139534760 true] [17592186308247 1089 "q-121714" 13194139534760 true] [17592186308247 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534760 true] [17592186308247 1100 "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨{e}^{{t}^{2}-1},2-5t⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $v.$" 13194139534760 true] [17592186308247 1113 #uuid "ccee9cb0-6d5e-5df1-a880-6088579e51f6" 13194139534760 true] [17592186308247 1145 "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{{t}^{2}-1}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2-5t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t{e}^{{t}^{2}-1},-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534760 true] [17592186308248 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308249 13194139534760 true] [17592186308248 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308250 13194139534760 true] [17592186308248 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308251 13194139534760 true] [17592186308248 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308252 13194139534760 true] [17592186308248 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308253 13194139534760 true] [17592186308248 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534760 true] [17592186308248 1041 "selection" 13194139534760 true] [17592186308248 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308250 13194139534760 true] [17592186308248 1110 #uuid "684fc375-4774-502f-934b-323e3d4abff7" 13194139534760 true] [17592186308249 1034 "v=⟨{e}^{{t}^{2}-1},2⟩" 13194139534760 true] [17592186308249 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534760 true] [17592186308249 1111 #uuid "8d61de6e-3918-5859-a37e-70330c865b87" 13194139534760 true] [17592186308250 1034 "v=⟨2t{e}^{{t}^{2}-1},-5⟩" 13194139534760 true] [17592186308250 1103 #edb/