, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-3t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2}+6t-3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2}-3,4t+6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3({t}^{2}-1),2(2t+3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3(t-1)(t+1),2(2t+3)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when its velocity is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨3(t-1)(t+1),2(2t+3)⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(t-1)(t+1)=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=\\pm 1, \\\\ 2(2t+3)=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is no value of $t$ that satisfies both equations, so there are no stationary points." 13194139534760 true] [17592186308276 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308277 13194139534760 true] [17592186308276 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308278 13194139534760 true] [17592186308276 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308279 13194139534760 true] [17592186308276 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308280 13194139534760 true] [17592186308276 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308281 13194139534760 true] [17592186308276 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534760 true] [17592186308276 1041 "selection" 13194139534760 true] [17592186308276 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308280 13194139534760 true] [17592186308276 1110 #uuid "333d07b7-e297-52fc-8269-a583519011b1" 13194139534760 true] [17592186308277 1034 "t=1" 13194139534760 true] [17592186308277 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534760 true] [17592186308277 1111 #uuid "9dbae6bb-bb43-5bc0-b002-a4e5c364a4c5" 13194139534760 true] [17592186308278 1034 "t=2" 13194139534760 true] [17592186308278 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534760 true] [17592186308278 1111 #uuid "207bcb60-0693-51c7-aba8-96defca8dfd8" 13194139534760 true] [17592186308279 1034 "t=4" 13194139534760 true] [17592186308279 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534760 true] [17592186308279 1111 #uuid "aae818a5-822e-555c-b2ef-1bed058b0416" 1319